{%- comment -%}
  z-[45] deliberately, NOT z-[100].

  This banner is fixed to the bottom of the viewport on every page. At z-[100] it
  outranked every overlay in the theme, including the cart drawer (z-[70]). On a
  375x667 phone the banner occupies the bottom 90px and the drawer's PROCEED TO
  CHECKOUT button sits at y 592-648 — entirely underneath it. document.elementFromPoint
  at the button's centre returned the banner, and a real tap did nothing: the store
  could not be checked out from on a phone until the shopper happened to dismiss
  cookies first.

  45 keeps the banner above ordinary page content and the filter-drawer overlay
  (z-40) while sitting below the filter drawer and header (z-50), the cart overlay
  and mobile nav (z-[60]), and the cart drawer itself (z-[70]). Consent is
  important; it is not more important than being able to pay.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div id="cookie-consent-banner"
  class="fixed bottom-0 left-0 right-0 z-[45] bg-deep text-cream transform translate-y-0 transition-transform duration-300"
  role="complementary"
  aria-label="Cookie consent">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between px-6 py-3 gap-3">
    <p class="font-body text-sm text-cream">We use cookies to improve your experience and for analytics.</p>
    <div class="flex gap-3 shrink-0">
      <button id="cookie-accept"
        class="bg-coral text-cream px-4 py-2 text-xs font-body uppercase tracking-wider">
        Accept
      </button>
      <button id="cookie-decline"
        class="border border-cream text-cream px-4 py-2 text-xs font-body">
        Decline
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<script type="module" src="{{ 'cookie-consent.js' | asset_url }}"></script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Cookie Consent",
  "settings": [],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Cookie Consent" }]
}
{% endschema %}
